# Is the declared incompatibility with Compact Work Tab still real?
#
# About.xml names Mlie.CompactWorkTab in <incompatibleWith>. Like the Work Tab set beside it, this
# one is built to go and look rather than to trust a declaration nobody has replayed.
#
# Read green-is-good, like every other set: the scenarios assert the DOCUMENTED SYMPTOM, with
# @allow-errors so the expected error does not fail them by itself. Green means the
# incompatibility is still what About.xml claims; red means something moved. An expected red and
# an accidental red are the same colour, which is why the suite is not simply let go red.
#
# Those scenarios are NOT written yet; the first run of this set plays the ordinary suite, which
# is exploration rather than validation.
#
# Replayed when COMPACT WORK TAB moves, not when Work Studio is published.
#
# packageId read from the installed copy's own About.xml, 2026-09-21.
#
# Not covered by this set, and not covered by About.xml either: captainarbitrary.compactworktab
# (Workshop 3027381000), the original this one continues. It carries a DIFFERENT packageId, so
# <incompatibleWith> stays silent for anyone who still has it installed from before the handover.
# Whether that deserves a line in About.xml is a judgement about who still runs it, not about
# whether it is abandoned - and it needs its own set either way, since the two cannot be staged
# together any more than the other pairs can.
#
# packageId             workshopId   what it is
Mlie.CompactWorkTab     3250322299   Compact Work Tab (Continued), the declared incompatibility
